        title="EST vs EDT Timeline" 
        loading="lazy" 
        decoding="async" 
        width="800" 
        height="400" 
        style="width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px;"
      />
      <figcaption class="infographic-caption">
        <strong>Figure 3: EST and EDT Transition Cycle.</strong> Timeline showing when New York transitions from Eastern Standard Time (EST) to Eastern Daylight Time (EDT) and back.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="warning-box">
      <strong>Warning:</strong> During the summer, New York operates on UTC-4 (EDT), not UTC-5 (EST). 
      Referring to New York's time as "EST" in July is technically incorrect and can cause scheduling errors for international teams who assume a standard UTC-5 offset.
    </div>

    <!-- Visual Asset 6: UTC Offset Infographic -->
