      <figcaption class="infographic-caption">
        <strong>Figure 10: New York Annual Clock Cycle.</strong> Diagram illustrating the yearly cycle of clock changes and the duration of standard (EST) and daylight (EDT) periods.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="did-you-know">
      <h4>Did You Know? The Sunshine Protection Act</h4>
      <p>
        In recent years, U.S. legislators have debated the Sunshine Protection Act, a bill that would make Daylight Saving Time permanent across the nation. 
        If passed, New York would remain on UTC-4 (EDT) year-round and would no longer adjust its clocks in March and November. 
        While the bill has received strong support, it has not yet been enacted into law. 
        For details on daylight transitions globally, see our guide on <a href="/daylight-saving-time-explained/">Daylight Saving Time Explained</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

