        <strong>Figure 4: Wall Street Trading Hours.</strong> Infographic displaying core, pre-market, and after-hours trading sessions on the NYSE and NASDAQ in Eastern Time.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Core Stock Market Hours:</strong> The New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) and NASDAQ operate their main trading sessions from **9:30 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. Eastern Time**, Monday through Friday.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Extended Trading:</strong> Pre-market sessions operate from 4:00 a.m. to 9:30 a.m. ET, and after-hours sessions run from 4:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m. ET.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Banking Hours:</strong> Major commercial banks in New York generally open from 9:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. ET. 
        International wire transfers and clearing houses (like CHIPS) coordinate their daily settlements around these Eastern Time operating windows.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

