    <h2>6. Travel &amp; Daily Life in NYC</h2>
    <p>
      If you are flying to New York, you will land at one of the region's major airports: John F. Kennedy International (JFK), LaGuardia (LGA), or Newark Liberty International (EWR). 
      Airline tickets are always printed in local times.
    </p>

    <!-- Visual Asset 8: Travel Time Difference Graphic -->
    <figure style="margin: 2.5rem 0; text-align: center; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
      <img 
        src="/assets/new-york-travel-time-difference.webp" 
        alt="Travel Time Adjustments to New York showing LA to NY and London to NY flights" 
        title="Travel Time Difference Graphic" 
        loading="lazy" 
        decoding="async" 
        width="800" 
        height="400" 
        style="width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px;"
      />
      <figcaption class="infographic-caption">
        <strong>Figure 8: New York Flight Time Adjustments.</strong> Visual guide displaying time adjustments required when traveling to New York from the West Coast or Europe.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>West Coast Travelers:</strong> Flying from Los Angeles (PT) to New York (ET) involves a 3-hour time jump forward. 
        If you depart LAX at 8:00 a.m., local time in New York is already 11:00 a.m. 
        Accounting for a 5.5-hour flight, you will land at JFK at 4:30 p.m. local time, which can make the travel day feel very short.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Eastward Jet Lag:</strong> Traveling from California or Asia to New York can cause eastward jet lag. 
        To adjust your biological clock, expose yourself to early morning daylight in New York and avoid caffeine in the late afternoon.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tourism Coordination:</strong> Broadway theater performances, museum hours (like the Met or MoMA), and public transport services operate on Eastern Time. 
        Ensure you synchronize your mobile devices to prevent missing your showtime.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

